4.text:
J. Impossible to tell from the given statement, in the literal system described.

C is nectar caffeine concentration. Citrus × sinensis, the orange, does not constitutively synthesize caffeine in nectar or in any other tissue in the wild. Background C in an orange is effectively 0 and remains 0 after a “knock-out of caffeine production”. The experimental manipulation Cexp ≡ Cctrl ≡ 0 therefore creates no contrast in the putative cause, and no contrast in the downstream mediators F and R or in Y that can be attributed to C. The path coefficients a,b,c,d,e are not identifiable in this species.

The sign pattern that is normally quoted for the caffeine-nectar causal mechanism that the diagram was derived from - e.g. Coffea spp. and other caffeine producing systems - is

* c > 0 : nectar caffeine increases learned fidelity / return rate, C ↑ → R ↑;
* d > 0 : pollinator retention is pollination enhancing, R ↑ → Y ↑;
* a < 0 : the stimulant/memory-enhancing effect shortens mean flower-level handling/foraging duration, C ↑ → F ↓;
* b < 0 : at the orchard/plant scale longer per-flower handling reduces flower throughput, i.e. F ↑ → Y ↓, so a- × b- gives a net positive C → F → Y indirect effect;
* e < 0 : caffeine / methylxanthine biosynthesis is a metabolic/resource cost with no direct physiological benefit to fruit set, C ↑ → Y ↓ directly.

That is the a –, b –, c +, d +, e – pattern, option B, and it is the literature-consistent mechanistic expectation for a caffeine producing plant. In a true caffeine producer a caffeine knock-out would be predicted to lower R, raise F and remove a direct metabolic cost, with a net loss of the pollinator-mediated yield benefit.

In oranges the manipulation does not generate the required variation in C, so the signs cannot be tested here.

6.text:
J. Impossible to tell from the given statement.

The sign pattern of a is a property of the causal mechanism C → … → Y. It is identifiable only if the manipulation actually generates contrast in the putative cause.

C is nectar caffeine concentration. Citrus × sinensis, the sweet orange used in commercial production, does not constitutively synthesise caffeine in nectar or in any other tissue in the wild. The background level of C in an orange is effectively zero. “Knocking out caffeine production” in a background that never makes caffeine therefore leaves

Cexp ≡ Cctrl ≡ 0

so no contrast in C is generated and no contrast is generated in the downstream mediators F and R. The five path coefficients a, b, c, d, e are not identifiable in this species system and the experiment as stated is ecologically meaningless.

That is not to say the model is vacuous. In the biological system where the model was derived, e.g. Coffea spp., the literature signs that are normally quoted are

* c > 0  caffeine increases learned fidelity / pollinator retention;
* d > 0  greater retention increases per-plant pollination and total yield;
* a < 0  the stimulant / reward-enhancing effect of caffeine shortens mean flower-level handling / foraging duration F;
* b < 0  a longer mean F, at fixed overall foraging time, reduces the number of flowers visited and hence system-level pollination throughput, so F → Y is negative in the sign convention used;
* e < 0  caffeine / methylxanthine biosynthesis is a metabolic / resource cost to the plant.

That is the a : –, b : –, c : +, d : +, e : – pattern, option B, that is the textbook caffeine-as-memory-enhancer / handling-time trade-off for the coffee-pollinator system. In a true orange background the manipulation cannot test it.

